<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Kaqchikel kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1470 CE – 1530 CE (approx.) · capital Iximche</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A highland Maya kingdom that broke from the K'iche' around 1470, allied with the Spanish in 1524 and then fought them for six years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaqchikel-people">Kaqchikel</a> had been allies and subjects of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kiche-kingdom">K'iche' kingdom</a>. Around 1470, during disputes that followed the reign of K'iq'ab, Kaqchikel lords left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qumarkaj">Q'umarkaj</a> and founded their own capital at Iximche, on a ridge in the central highlands, becoming an independent and expanding power.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Iximche held palaces, temples and ballcourts in walled plazas for the leading lineages, whose two chief lords ruled jointly. The kingdom fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiche-people">K'iche'</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tzutujil-people">Tz'utujil</a> kingdoms. Its history, from origin myths to the Spanish conquest, is recorded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-the-kaqchikels">Annals of the Kaqchikels</a>, written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaqchikel-people">Kaqchikel</a> in the colonial period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaqchikel-people">Kaqchikel</a> kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaji-imox">Kaji' Imox</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beleheb-kat">Beleheb' Kat</a> welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-alvarado">Pedro de Alvarado</a> in 1524, and Iximche briefly became the first Spanish capital. Harsh demands led to a revolt that ended in 1530; Kaji' Imox was hanged in 1540. Kaqchikel remains widely spoken.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kaqchikel-kingdom.jpg" alt="Kaqchikel kingdom" width="320" height="238"><figcaption>Image: Reinhard Jahn, Mannheim nanosmile Wikipedia account please use this discussion page · CC BY-SA 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chichicastenango-004.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1470 CE – 1530 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Iximche</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kaji' Imox, Beleheb' Kat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kaqchikel</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Guatemala</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cakchiquel kingdom, Iximche</dd></dl></aside></div>
